eck: Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group.); [medium] Consumer errors causing repeated rebalances (next check: Check consumer group status for errors or rebalances.); [medium] Hot partition / key skew concentrating load (next check: Analyze partition distribution and load metrics.)\n\n## 3. Correlation (A2)\ncandidate=incident-001; correlated_signals=['sig-sample', 'consumer_lag']; dependency_path=Payments Settlement -> consumer throughput -> consumer group status\n\n## 4. Priority / Severity (A3)\nP2 - The consumer lag of 60000 messages exceeds the static threshold of 50000, indicating a likely issue with downstream processing, which could lead to delayed or failed payments.\n\n## 5. Remediation recommendation (A5)\n  - Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group. (approval_required=True; verify: Throughput metrics should show if the consumer is processing at expected rates.; rollback: No rollback needed as this is a read-only diagnostic.)\n  - Check consumer group status for errors or rebalances. (approval_required=True; verify: Consumer group status should indicate any errors or rebalances.; rollback: No rollback needed as this is a read-only diagnostic.)\n  - Analyze partition distribution and load metrics. (approval_required=True; verify: Partition metrics should show if load is evenly distributed.; rollback: No rollback needed as this is a read-only diagnostic.)\n  - Check the number of consumer instances against the partition count. (approval_required=True; verify: Comparison of consumer instances and partition count should indicate adequacy.; rollback: No rollback needed as this is a read-only diagnostic.)\n\n## 6. Business impact\nPayments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk\n\n## 7. Stakeholders to notify\n  - app_owner: payments-app-owner@example.com\n  - business_owner: payments-biz-owner@example.com\n  - prod_support: prodsupport-payments@example.com\n  - sre: sre-streaming@example.com\n  - on_call: pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments\n"}, "a7": {"recipients_by_role": {"app_owner": "payments-app-owner@example.com", "business_owner": "payments-biz-owner@example.com", "prod_support": "prodsupport-payments@example.com", "sre": "sre-streaming@example.com", "on_call": "pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments"}, "message": "Attention: A consumer lag of 60,000 messages has been detected in the Payments Settlement service, exceeding the static threshold of 50,000. This situation poses a risk of delayed or failed payments and potential settlement backlogs. Immediate investigation is required to assess consumer throughput and check for errors or rebalances in the consumer group. Please prioritize this issue as it is classified as a P2 severity incident.", "channel": "email", "escalation_reason": "Critical service degradation due to high consumer lag affecting payment processing.", "delivery_status": "not_sent"}, "a8": {"recovery_status": "monitoring", "metrics_before_after": {"consumer_lag_before": 60000, "consumer_lag_after": null}, "closure_recommendation": "continue_monitoring", "feedback_record": {"incident_id": "incident-001", "summary": "Consumer lag remains at 60,000 messages, exceeding the threshold of 50,000. Further investigation is required to determine the root cause and implement remediation.", "next_steps": ["Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group.", "Check consumer group status for errors or rebalances.", "Analyze partition distribution and load metrics.", "Check the number of consumer instances against the partition count."]}}}}
