ompare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group.); [0.6] Consumer errors causing repeated rebalances (next check: Check consumer group status for errors or rebalances.); [0.5] Hot partition / key skew concentrating load (next check: Analyze partition load distribution metrics.)\n\n## 3. Correlation (A2)\ncandidate=incident-001; correlated_signals=['sig-sample', 'consumer_lag']; dependency_path=Payments Settlement -> consumer_lag\n\n## 4. Priority / Severity (A3)\nP2 - The consumer lag of 60000 messages exceeds the static threshold of 50000, indicating a likely issue with downstream processing, which could lead to delayed or failed payments and regulatory risks.\n\n## 5. Remediation recommendation (A5)\n  - Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group. (approval_required=True; verify: Throughput and input rates are compared and analyzed.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n  - Check consumer group status for errors or rebalances. (approval_required=True; verify: Review consumer group status for any reported errors or rebalances.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n  - Analyze partition load distribution metrics. (approval_required=True; verify: Review partition load distribution metrics for any imbalances.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n  - Review the number of consumer instances relative to the partition count. (approval_required=True; verify: Compare the number of consumer instances to the number of partitions.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n\n## 6. Business impact\nPayments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk\n\n## 7. Stakeholders to notify\n  - app_owner: payments-app-owner@example.com\n  - business_owner: payments-biz-owner@example.com\n  - prod_support: prodsupport-payments@example.com\n  - sre: sre-streaming@example.com\n  - on_call: pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments\n"}, "a7": {"recipients_by_role": {"app_owner": "payments-app-owner@example.com", "business_owner": "payments-biz-owner@example.com", "prod_support": "prodsupport-payments@example.com", "sre": "sre-streaming@example.com", "on_call": "pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments"}, "message": "", "channel": "", "escalation_reason": null, "delivery_status": "not_sent"}, "a8": {"recovery_status": "monitoring", "metrics_before_after": {"consumer_lag_before": 60000, "consumer_lag_after": null}, "closure_recommendation": "continue_monitoring", "feedback_record": {"incident_id": "incident-001", "summary": "A consumer lag of 60,000 messages has been detected in the Payments Settlement service, exceeding the static threshold of 50,000. This situation poses a risk of delayed or failed payments and potential regulatory issues. Investigations are needed to determine if the downstream consumer is slow, if there are consumer errors, or if there are insufficient consumer instances.", "business_impact": "Payments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk", "next_steps": ["Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group.", "Check consumer group status for errors or rebalances.", "Analyze partition load distribution metrics.", "Review the number of consumer instances relative to the partition count."]}}}}
