itions.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)", "Review the number of consumer instances versus the partition count. (approval_required=True; verify: Compare the number of consumer instances to the number of partitions.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)"], "business_impact": "Payments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk", "stakeholders": {"app_owner": "payments-app-owner@example.com", "business_owner": "payments-biz-owner@example.com", "prod_support": "prodsupport-payments@example.com", "sre": "sre-streaming@example.com", "on_call": "pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments"}, "timeline": ["signal received", "validated (A1)", "correlated (A2)", "severity assessed (A3)", "RCA (A4)", "remediation proposed (A5)", "incident recorded (A6)"], "evidence_links": ["metric:consumer_lag", "runbooks.md :: RB-01 — Consumer lag rising", "escalation_guidelines.md :: P2 / High"], "ticket_payload": {"incident_id": "incident-001", "severity": "P2", "entity": "topic:payments.settlement", "issue": "topic:payments.settlement: consumer_lag = 60000 messages (classification: likely, anomaly_score: 0.635) in prod.", "business_impact": "Payments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk"}, "closure_document": "# Incident incident-001\n\n**Summary:** A consumer lag of 60,000 messages has been detected in the Payments Settlement service, exceeding the static threshold of 50,000 messages. This situation is classified as P2 severity, indicating potential delays or failures in payments and a settlement backlog, which poses SLA and regulatory risks. Recommended next steps include investigating consumer throughput versus input rates and checking the consumer group status for errors.\n\n## 1. Issue (from signal)\ntopic:payments.settlement: consumer_lag = 60000 messages (classification: likely, anomaly_score: 0.635) in prod.\n\n## 2. Root-cause analysis (A4)\n[0.8] Downstream consumer slow or under-capacity (next check: Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group.); [0.6] Consumer errors causing repeated rebalances (next check: Check consumer group status for errors or rebalances.); [0.5] Hot partition / key skew concentrating load (next check: Analyze partition load distribution and consumer assignment.)\n\n## 3. Correlation (A2)\ncandidate=incident-001; correlated_signals=['sig-sample', 'consumer_lag']; dependency_path=Payments Settlement -> consumer_lag\n\n## 4. Priority / Severity (A3)\nP2 - The consumer lag of 60000 messages exceeds the static threshold of 50000, indicating a likely issue that could lead to delayed or failed payments and regulatory risks.\n\n## 5. Remediation recommendation (A5)\n  - Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group. (approval_required=True; verify: Throughput metrics should be compared to input rates.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n  - Check consumer group status for errors or rebalances. (approval_required=True; verify: Check for any reported errors or rebalances in the consumer group.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n  - Analyze partition load distribution and consumer assignment. (approval_required=True; verify: Review the load distribution metrics across partitions.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n  - Review the number of consumer instances versus the partition count. (approval_required=True; verify: Compare the number of consumer instances to the number of partitions.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n\n## 6. Business impact\nPayments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk\n\n## 7. Stakeholders to notify\n  - app_owner: payments-app-owner@example.com\n  - business_owner: payments-biz-owner@example.com\n  - prod_support: prodsupport-payments@example.com\n  - sre: sre-streaming@example.com\n  - on_call: pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments\n"}, "a7": {"recipients_by_role": {"app_owner": "payments-app-owner@example.com", "business_owner": "payments-biz-owner@example.com", "prod_support": "prodsupport-payments@example.com", "sre": "sre-streaming@example.com", "on_call": "pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments"}, "message": "Attention: A consumer lag of 60,000 messages has been detected in the Payments Settlement service, exceeding the static threshold of 50,000 messages. This situation is classified as P2 severity, indicating potential delays or failures in payments and a settlement backlog, which poses SLA and regulatory risks. Immediate investigation is required to compare consumer throughput versus input rates and check the consumer group status for errors.", "channel": "email", "escalation_reason": "Critical consumer lag impacting payment processing and regulatory compliance.", "delivery_status": "not_sent"}, "a8": {"recovery_status": "monitoring", "metrics_before_after": {"consumer_lag_before": 60000, "consumer_lag_after": null}, "closure_recommendation": "continue_monitoring", "feedback_record": {"incident_id": "incident-001", "summary": "Consumer lag remains at 60,000 messages, exceeding the threshold of 50,000. Further investigation is required to determine root causes and implement remediation steps.", "next_steps": ["Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group.", "Check consumer group status for errors or rebalances.", "Analyze partition load distribution and consumer assignment.", "Review the number of consumer instances versus the partition count."]}}}}
