umer lag of 60,000 messages has been detected in the Payments Settlement service, exceeding the static threshold of 50,000, indicating potential issues with downstream processing. This situation poses a risk of delayed or failed payments and may lead to a settlement backlog and SLA/regulatory risks. Recommended next steps include investigating consumer throughput versus input rates and checking for errors or rebalances in the consumer group.", "issue": "topic:payments.settlement: consumer_lag = 60000 messages (classification: likely, anomaly_score: 0.635) in prod.", "root_cause": "[0.8] Downstream consumer slow or under-capacity (next check: Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group.); [0.5] Consumer errors causing repeated rebalances (next check: Check consumer group for errors or rebalances.); [0.4] Hot partition / key skew concentrating load (next check: Analyze partition load distribution.)", "correlation": "candidate=incident-001; correlated_signals=['sig-sample', 'consumer_lag:60000', 'produce_error_rate:spike']; dependency_path=Payments Settlement -> Downstream Consumer -> Producer", "severity": "P2", "severity_rationale": "The consumer lag of 60000 messages exceeds the static threshold of 50000, indicating a likely issue with downstream processing, which could lead to delayed or failed payments.", "remediation": ["Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group. (approval_required=True; verify: Throughput metrics should be available for comparison.; rollback: No rollback necessary; this is a read-only action.)", "Check consumer group for errors or rebalances. (approval_required=True; verify: Check logs for errors or rebalance events.; rollback: No rollback necessary; this is a read-only action.)", "Analyze partition load distribution. (approval_required=True; verify: Review partition metrics for load distribution.; rollback: No rollback necessary; this is a read-only action.)", "Review the number of consumer instances relative to partition count. (approval_required=True; verify: Check the ratio of consumer instances to partitions.; rollback: No rollback necessary; this is a read-only action.)"], "business_impact": "Payments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk", "stakeholders": {"app_owner": "payments-app-owner@example.com", "business_owner": "payments-biz-owner@example.com", "prod_support": "prodsupport-payments@example.com", "sre": "sre-streaming@example.com", "on_call": "pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments"}, "timeline": ["signal received", "validated (A1)", "correlated (A2)", "severity assessed (A3)", "RCA (A4)", "remediation proposed (A5)", "incident recorded (A6)"], "evidence_links": ["metric:consumer_lag", "runbooks.md :: RB-01 — Consumer lag rising", "escalation_guidelines.md :: P2 / High"], "ticket_payload": {"incident_id": "incident-001", "severity": "P2", "entity": "topic:payments.settlement", "issue": "topic:payments.settlement: consumer_lag = 60000 messages (classification: likely, anomaly_score: 0.635) in prod.", "business_impact": "Payments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk"}, "closure_document": "# Incident incident-001\n\n**Summary:** A consumer lag of 60,000 messages has been detected in the Payments Settlement service, exceeding the static threshold of 50,000, indicating potential issues with downstream processing. This situation poses a risk of delayed or failed payments and may lead to a settlement backlog and SLA/regulatory risks. Recommended next steps include investigating consumer throughput versus input rates and checking for errors or rebalances in the consumer group.\n\n## 1. Issue (from signal)\ntopic:payments.settlement: consumer_lag = 60000 messages (classification: likely, anomaly_score: 0.635) in prod.\n\n## 2. Root-cause analysis (A4)\n[0.8] Downstream consumer slow or under-capacity (next check: Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group.); [0.5] Consumer errors causing repeated rebalances (next check: Check consumer group for errors or rebalances.); [0.4] Hot partition / key skew concentrating load (next check: Analyze partition load distribution.)\n\n## 3. Correlation (A2)\ncandidate=incident-001; correlated_signals=['sig-sample', 'consumer_lag:60000', 'produce_error_rate:spike']; dependency_path=Payments Settlement -> Downstream Consumer -> Producer\n\n## 4. Priority / Severity (A3)\nP2 - The consumer lag of 60000 messages exceeds the static threshold of 50000, indicating a likely issue with downstream processing, which could lead to delayed or failed payments.\n\n## 5. Remediation recommendation (A5)\n  - Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group. (approval_required=True; verify: Throughput metrics should be available for comparison.; rollback: No rollback necessary; this is a read-only action.)\n  - Check consumer group for errors or rebalances. (approval_required=True; verify: Check logs for errors or rebalance events.; rollback: No rollback necessary; this is a read-only action.)\n  - Analyze partition load distribution. (approval_required=True; verify: Review partition metrics for load distribution.; rollback: No rollback necessary; this is a read-only action.)\n  - Review the number of consumer instances relative to partition count. (approval_required=True; verify: Check the ratio of consumer instances to partitions.; rollback: No rollback necessary; this is a read-only action.)\n\n## 6. Business impact\nPayments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk\n\n## 7. Stakeholders to notify\n  - app_owner: payments-app-owner@example.com\n  - business_owner: payments-biz-owner@example.com\n  - prod_support: prodsupport-payments@example.com\n  - sre: sre-streaming@example.com\n  - on_call: pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments\n"}, "a7": {"recipients_by_role": {"app_owner": "payments-app-owner@example.com", "business_owner": "payments-biz-owner@example.com", "prod_support": "prodsupport-payments@example.com", "sre": "sre-streaming@example.com", "on_call": "pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments"}, "message": "A consumer lag of 60,000 messages has been detected in the Payments Settlement service, exceeding the static threshold of 50,000. This indicates potential issues with downstream processing, posing a risk of delayed or failed payments, and may lead to a settlement backlog and SLA/regulatory risks. Immediate investigation is required to compare consumer throughput versus input rates and check for errors or rebalances in the consumer group.", "channel": "email", "escalation_reason": "Critical degradation of the Payments Settlement service due to high consumer lag.", "delivery_status": "not_sent"}, "a8": {"recovery_status": "monitoring", "metrics_before_after": {"consumer_lag_before": 60000, "consumer_lag_after": null}, "closure_recommendation": "continue_monitoring", "feedback_record": {"incident_id": "incident-001", "summary": "The consumer lag remains at 60,000 messages, indicating ongoing issues with downstream processing. Further investigation is required to determine the root cause and implement necessary remediation steps.", "next_steps": ["Continue monitoring consumer lag metrics.", "Investigate consumer throughput versus input rates.", "Check for errors or rebalances in the consumer group."]}}}}
