ors or rebalances.); [medium] Hot partition / key skew concentrating load (next check: Analyze partition distribution and load metrics.)\n\n## 3. Correlation (A2)\ncandidate=incident-001; correlated_signals=['sig-sample', 'consumer_lag:60000', 'produce_error_rate:spike']; dependency_path=Payments Settlement -> Downstream Consumer -> Producer\n\n## 4. Priority / Severity (A3)\nP2 - The consumer lag of 60000 messages exceeds the static threshold of 50000, indicating a likely issue with downstream processing, which could lead to delayed or failed payments and regulatory risks.\n\n## 5. Remediation recommendation (A5)\n  - Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group. (approval_required=True; verify: Throughput metrics should be available in monitoring tools.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a diagnostic step.)\n  - Check consumer group status for errors or rebalances. (approval_required=True; verify: Consumer group status should indicate any errors or rebalances.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a diagnostic step.)\n  - Analyze partition distribution and load metrics. (approval_required=True; verify: Partition metrics should be available in monitoring tools.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a diagnostic step.)\n  - Review the number of consumer instances relative to partition count. (approval_required=True; verify: Instance and partition metrics should be available in monitoring tools.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a diagnostic step.)\n\n## 6. Business impact\nPayments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk\n\n## 7. Stakeholders to notify\n  - app_owner: payments-app-owner@example.com\n  - business_owner: payments-biz-owner@example.com\n  - prod_support: prodsupport-payments@example.com\n  - sre: sre-streaming@example.com\n  - on_call: pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments\n"}, "a7": {"recipients_by_role": {"app_owner": "payments-app-owner@example.com", "business_owner": "payments-b