ad balancing.)", "correlation": "candidate=incident-001; correlated_signals=['sig-002', 'consumer_lag']; dependency_path=fraud.scoring", "severity": "P2", "severity_rationale": "The consumer lag of 90000 messages exceeds the static threshold of 50000, indicating a likely issue with the fraud scoring consumer group that could delay fraud detection.", "remediation": ["Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group. (approval_required=True; verify: Throughput metrics should be compared and analyzed.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)", "Check consumer group for any errors or rebalances. (approval_required=True; verify: Review logs for errors or rebalance events.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)", "Investigate partition distribution and load balancing. (approval_required=True; verify: Analyze partition load and distribution metrics.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)"], "business_impact": "Fraud scoring delayed; potential unscored fraud exposure in ATM/card transactions", "stakeholders": {"app_owner": "fraud-app-owner@example.com", "business_owner": "fraud-biz-owner@example.com", "prod_support": "prodsupport-fraud@example.com", "sre": "sre-ml@example.com", "on_call": "pager:fraud-oncall / #inc-fraud"}, "timeline": ["signal received", "validated (A1)", "correlated (A2)", "severity assessed (A3)", "RCA (A4)", "remediation proposed (A5)", "incident recorded (A6)"], "evidence_links": ["metric:consumer_lag"], "ticket_payload": {"incident_id": "incident-001", "severity": "P2", "entity": "consumer_group:fraud.scoring", "issue": "consumer_group:fraud.scoring: consumer_lag = 90000 messages (classification: likely, anomaly_score: 0.667) in prod.", "business_impact": "Fraud scoring delayed; potential unscored fraud exposure in ATM/card transactions"}, "closure_document": "# Incident incident-001\n\n**Summary:** The fraud scoring consumer group is experiencing a significan