s.)\n\n## 3. Correlation (A2)\ncandidate=incident-001; correlated_signals=['sig-sample', 'signal-consumer_lag']; dependency_path=Payments Settlement -> consumer_lag\n\n## 4. Priority / Severity (A3)\nP2 - The consumer lag of 60000 messages exceeds the static threshold of 50000, indicating a likely issue with downstream processing or consumer capacity.\n\n## 5. Remediation recommendation (A5)\n  - Compare consumer throughput vs input (produce) rate for the group. (approval_required=True; verify: Throughput metrics should be available for comparison.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n  - Check consumer group performance for errors or rebalances. (approval_required=True; verify: Check for any reported errors or rebalances in the consumer group.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n  - Analyze partition load distribution metrics. (approval_required=True; verify: Review metrics for any signs of skew or uneven load.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n  - Review the number of consumer instances relative to partition count. (approval_required=True; verify: Check the ratio of consumer instances to partition count.; rollback: No rollback necessary as this is a read-only action.)\n\n## 6. Business impact\nPayments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk\n\n## 7. Stakeholders to notify\n  - app_owner: payments-app-owner@example.com\n  - business_owner: payments-biz-owner@example.com\n  - prod_support: prodsupport-payments@example.com\n  - sre: sre-streaming@example.com\n  - on_call: pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments\n"}, "a7": {"recipients_by_role": {"app_owner": "payments-app-owner@example.com", "business_owner": "payments-biz-owner@example.com", "prod_support": "prodsupport-payments@example.com", "sre": "sre-streaming@example.com", "on_call": "pager:payments-oncall / #inc-payments"}, "message": "Attention: A consumer lag of 60,000 messages has been detected in the Payments Settlement service, exceeding the static threshold of 50,000 messages. This situation poses a risk of delayed or failed payments, leading to a settlement backlog and potential SLA/regulatory issues. Immediate diagnostics are recommended to assess consumer throughput and performance.", "channel": "email", "escalation_reason": "Critical consumer lag impacting payment processing.", "delivery_status": "not_sent"}, "a8": {"recovery_status": "monitoring", "metrics_before_after": {"consumer_lag_before": 60000, "consumer_lag_after": 60000}, "closure_recommendation": "continue_monitoring", "feedback_record": {"incident_id": "incident-001", "summary": "The consumer lag remains at 60,000 messages, indicating that the issue with downstream processing or consumer capacity has not been resolved. Further diagnostics and remediation actions are required.", "business_impact": "Payments delayed or failed; settlement backlog; SLA/regulatory risk", "next_steps": ["Continue monitoring consumer lag metrics.", "Engage with the downstream consumer team to address capacity issues.", "Perform diagnostics as recommended in the remediation plan."]}}}}
